# Evidence tree: deny by default, allow text only (`D41`, P0.T28).
# Binaries live in /Users/alex/fine-line-data/open-toolchain-gw5ast/ and are
# referenced from a row by absolute path plus sha256 -- never committed here.
# git takes the WHOLE line as the pattern, so every justification is its own
# comment line, never a trailing one.
*
# Descend into slug directories so the allowlist below can be reached.
!*/
!.gitignore
# summary.md, evidence-table.md and any prose beside a runs.jsonl
!*.md
# the JSON Lines rows themselves (`spec-harness.md` §6)
!runs.jsonl
# text diffs quoted by summaries and PR bodies, at any depth
!**/diff/**
# the S22/V8 parity exception file
!parity-exceptions.tsv
# the chipdb sha256 ledger (P0.T15/T15b/T40) -- was silently untracked after the
# evidence-tree move (C10/D80): "*.txt" is allowed only under _runs/, and this file
# lives directly under evidence/chipdb/. Fixed on the spot (P0.T40).
!chipdb/chipdb-sha256.txt
# the D62 oracle-run ledger the clocking checkpoint reads (P1.T03), same
# named-exception pattern as chipdb-sha256.txt above: a .tsv is not covered
# by the "*.md" allowance and lives directly under evidence/_budget/.
!_budget/clocking-runs.tsv
# batch, watchdog and tool logs (`spec-harness.md` §8)
!_runs/*.log
# provenance stamps: sha256 lists, tool versions, gowinhome.selected
!_runs/*.txt
!_runs/*.selected
# the Licence Gate's provisional marker read by P0.T39 (F10, D52)
!_runs/*.flag
# _gates/ holds the detached local-gate's PASS/FAIL markers, logs, pidfiles
# and watchdog logs (C12/D94/D95) -- all machine-local, regenerated by every
# gate run, and already denied by the leading `*` above. Only the directory
# marker is allowed through, so a fresh checkout still has the directory for
# `.githooks/pre-push` to write into.
!_gates/.gitkeep
# the P1.T17 PLL-site enumeration: the machine-readable table P1.T18 reads,
# the attribute-id census the blueprint names, and the generator that produces
# both from the shipped .fse/.dat (committed beside its output so the
# enumeration is reproducible from the vendor files alone). Same named-exception
# pattern as chipdb-sha256.txt above -- .json/.tsv/.py are not covered by "*.md".
!plla/sites-138c.json
!plla/attrids-138c.tsv
!plla/gen_sites_138c.py
# the P1.T19 site trace: the analyser that turns each run's .fs into per-tile
# fuse counts, and its output -- the per-run bit census for all twelve
# candidate three-tile groups, which is the evidence behind the
# site-name -> anchor bijection in sites-138c.md section 8.
!plla/gen_trace_138c.py
!plla/runs/trace-138c.json
# the P1.T22 PLL attribute map: the analyser that reconciles the shipped
# .fse's logicinfo['PLL'] against attrids.py and attributes each oracle run's
# moved bits to an attribute, and its output -- the per-run moved-bit lists
# attrmap-138c.md's tables are read from. Same named-exception pattern as
# above; .json/.py are not covered by "*.md".
!plla/gen_attrmap_138c.py
!plla/attrmap-138c.json
# the batch resume ledger: one evidence row per executed run, the file
# `harness/README.md` names as `<batch_id>.rows.jsonl`. `!runs.jsonl` above
# matches that exact basename only, so the per-batch ledgers under _runs/
# were silently untracked.
!_runs/*.rows.jsonl
# the P1.T25 DHCEN control-pin trace: the campaign driver, the deterministic
# reduction from its raw output to the committed table, and that output itself.
# Same named-exception pattern as plla/ above -- .json/.jsonl/.py are not
# covered by "*.md", and trace-138c.md claims the reduction is auditable
# without re-running the oracle, which is only true if these are in the tree.
!dhcen/probe_dhce.py
!dhcen/build_ce_wires.py
!dhcen/ce-wires-138c.json
!dhcen/oracle-runs.jsonl
!dhcen/trace-result.json
!dhcen/trace-result-tieresetn.json
!dhcen/trace-result-control.json
!dhcen/trace-result-1620.json
!dhcen/trace-result-1719.json
!dhcen/fuse-presence-diff.json
!dhcen/fuse_probe.py
!dhcen/build_fuse_table.py
!dhcen/fuse-138c.json
# the P1.T27 DHCE lane campaign: the five-run vendor driver whose output
# lane-138c.md's site-index = lane-index table and the CLKDIV.RESETN
# measurement are both read off. Same named-exception pattern as the P1.T25/T26
# drivers above -- a .py is not covered by "*.md".
!dhcen/gate_probe.py
# the P1.T08d clock-mux campaign: the vendor-run driver, the two read-only
# decoders every number in mux38-138c.md comes out of, and the sha256 ledger
# of the 27 run .fs (D99 -- the .fs themselves are denied below and live in
# $DATASTORE). Same named-exception pattern as plla/ and dhcen/ above.
!hclk/staircase_blocks.py
!hclk/probe_clkmux.py
!hclk/e0_hclk_scope.py
!hclk/p1t08d-fs.sha256

# the P1.T28 DQCE/DCS tile-type re-derivation: the 8-run probe driver, the
# reduced-diff re-run script (the embedded diff in run_probe.py stalled on
# 16 incremental presence_diff calls and was killed; this 2-call script
# reproduces the numbers tiletypes-138c.md quotes), the oracle-run ledger,
# and the structured JSON both tiletypes-138c.md and tiles-138c.md are
# generated from. Same named-exception pattern as plla/ and dhcen/ above.
!dqce/run_probe.py
!dqce/diff_fast.py
!dqce/runs/oracle-runs.jsonl
!dqce/tiletypes-138c.json
!dcs/tiles-138c.json
# the P1.T23 PLL sweep batch A: the analyser that attributes each point's
# moved fuses and cross-checks them against P1.T22's attrmap, its output (the
# per-point moved-bit lists sweep-a-138c.md's table is read from), and the
# row-merge step P1.T41-T43 reuse to rewrite a batch's `sweep` map into the
# {axis, <parameter>} form the evidence schema wants. Same named-exception
# pattern as plla/ above -- .json/.py are not covered by "*.md".
!plla/gen_sweep_a_138c.py
!plla/merge_sweep_rows.py
!plla/sweep-a-138c.json

# the P1.T14 CLKDIV DIV_MODE sweep: the analyser that differences each run's
# vendor .fs inside the HCLK block cell, resolves the moved bits through the
# tile's shortval['HCLK'] table and cross-checks the result against what
# gowin_pack.GW5A.get_CLKDIV_fuses predicts, its output (the per-point moved-bit
# lists summary.md's fuse table is generated from), the batch-rows -> slug-rows
# promotion step and the table renderer summary.md's verdict table comes out of.
# Same named-exception pattern as plla/ and dhcen/ above -- .json/.py are not
# covered by "*.md", and summary.md claims its tables are generated rather than
# retyped, which is only checkable if these are in the tree.
!clkdiv/gen_divmode_fuses.py
!clkdiv/divmode-fuses-138c.json
!clkdiv/promote_rows.py
!clkdiv/row_table.py

# Explicitly denied, even under an allowed directory (last match wins):
*.fs
*.vo
*.tr
*.sdf
*.fse
*.dat
*.tm

# the P1.T41 PLL sweep batch B and the charge-pump campaign: the batch-B
# analyser and its output, the pump fitter and the fit itself, and the
# attribute decoder. sweep-b-138c.md and pump-138c.md both claim their tables
# are generated from these rather than retyped, and
# tests/test_gw5ast138c_plla.py::test_pll_pump_reproduces_every_measured_point
# reads pump-138c.json -- none of which holds on a fresh checkout while they
# are denied by the leading `*`. Untracked since P1.T41; fixed on the spot.
!plla/gen_sweep_b_138c.py
!plla/sweep-b-138c.json
!plla/gen_pump_138c.py
!plla/pump-138c.json
!plla/decode_pll_attrs_138c.py

# the P1.T42 PLL sweep batch C (the DYN modes and the loaded-CLKOUT1 ODIV1
# axis) and the P1.T43 twelve-site sweep: the analyser that attributes each
# batch-C point's moved fuses, the decoder that reads each site's attribute
# map out of its own bitstream, and both outputs -- the tables in
# sweep-c-138c.md and sites-e1-138c.md are read off these, and
# test_plla_sites_decode_identically_except_the_two_left_edge_sites asserts
# against sites-e1-138c.json. Same named-exception pattern as plla/ above.
!plla/gen_sweep_c_138c.py
!plla/sweep-c-138c.json
!plla/gen_sites_e1_138c.py
!plla/sites-e1-138c.json

# the P2.T02/T03 AE350 measurements: the machine-readable port inventory
# (149 ports, 911 bits, four sources reconciled) and the McuIns/McuOuts dump
# whose emptiness is the whole reconciliation verdict.
# tools/tests/test_ae350_evidence.py reads both, so on a fresh checkout the
# tests fail while they are denied by the leading `*`. Same named-exception
# pattern as plla/ and dhcen/ above -- .json is not covered by "*.md".
!ae350/port-inventory.json
!ae350/mcu-tables.json

# the P2.T26 AE350 wire map and its run ledger: the data file
# `fse_create_ae350()` reads (the measured footprint, the interface tile bands
# and the .dat table pointers), and the oracle-run ledger rescope.md's budget
# and tools/tests/test_ae350_wire_map.py both read. Same named-exception
# pattern as _budget/clocking-runs.tsv and ae350/port-inventory.json above --
# a .json or .tsv is not covered by "*.md".
!ae350/wire-map-138c.json
!_budget/ae350-runs.tsv
# the ae350-dualpins sub-ledger (P2.T29): same class as the two ledgers above --
# a .tsv directly under evidence/_budget/, which the "*.md" allowance misses.
!_budget/dualpin-runs.tsv
# the pip cross-check the wire map's MEASURED provenance rests on: the row-0
# taps run p2t26-tilewires' bitstream is seen to use, kept as its own input so
# that `tools/derive_ae350_wire_map.py` can regenerate the map from the .dat
# without the banked runs. Same named-exception pattern as
# ae350/wire-map-138c.json above.
!ae350/wire-map-pipdiff-138c.json
# the phase-close tree-clean check's RAW `git status --porcelain` output, kept
# verbatim beside the filtered one so the exclusion list hides nothing (the
# ratified V11 form). A .txt directly under a slug directory, so it needs the
# same named exception as chipdb-sha256.txt above.
!ae350/tree-status-raw.txt
# the AE350 port map of record: the machine-readable half of
# portmap-reconciled-138c.md, generated from the shipped chipdb by
# tools/derive_ae350_portmap_reconciled.py, whose --check mode is what keeps
# the two in step. Same named-exception pattern as ae350/wire-map-138c.json
# above -- a .json is not covered by "*.md".
!ae350/portmap-reconciled-138c.json
# the AE350 band-bit measurement: the two filters of
# tools/derive_ae350_band_bits.py over five AE350 bitstreams and the AE350-free
# control, which is what fuse-set-138c.md's table and
# tests/test_ae350_config_fuses.py both read. Same named exception as above.
!ae350/band-bits-138c.json

# the P3.T04 IOLOGIC ttyp adjudication: one row per candidate tile type with
# the verdict and the two criteria behind it, which
# tests/test_io_iologic_138c.py::test_iologic_ttyp_exclusion_138c_matches_evidence
# reads to check the literal in `fse_iologic` against the evidence. Same
# named-exception pattern as _budget/clocking-runs.tsv above -- a .tsv directly
# under a slug directory is not covered by "*.md".
!oddr-iddr/ttyp-adjudication.tsv

# the P3.T06/P3.T07 pin -> bank -> HCLK table: the machine-readable artefact
# `tools/derive_pin_hclk_138c.py --check` regenerates and
# tools/tests/test_pin_hclk_138c.py reads. It was silently untracked by P3.T06
# -- pin-hclk-138c.md claims it is the machine-readable half of itself, which
# is not true on a fresh checkout while it is denied by the leading `*`.
# Fixed on the spot. Same named-exception pattern as ae350/wire-map-138c.json.
!iologic/pin-hclk-138c.json
# the P3.T07 sweep driver: the twelve-ball vendor campaign and the decoder
# every block/lane number in pin-to-hclk/summary.md comes out of. Same
# named-exception pattern as hclk/probe_clkmux.py above -- a .py is not
# covered by "*.md", and the summary claims the table is decoded rather than
# retyped, which is only auditable if this is in the tree.
!pin-to-hclk/sweep_pin_hclk.py
# the Phase-3 oracle-run ledger, same class as _budget/clocking-runs.tsv and
# _budget/ae350-runs.tsv above.
!_budget/iologic-runs.tsv
# the P3.T11 ODDR/ODDRC/IDDR/IDDRC attribute audit: the driver that spends the
# task's two oracle runs and decodes them, and its three text artefacts. The
# summary's per-primitive attribute and fuse tables are read out of these, and
# tests/test_io_iologic_138c.py::test_oddr_iddr_attr_gap_recorded reads the
# .tsv, so a claim in the summary is only auditable with them in the tree.
# Same named-exception pattern as pin-to-hclk/sweep_pin_hclk.py above.
!oddr-iddr/audit_oddr_iddr_attrs.py
!oddr-iddr/attr-gap.tsv
!oddr-iddr/fuse-delta.json
!oddr-iddr/audit-runs.json
# the P3.T11 batch driver, beside the log it writes.
!_runs/p3-oddr-iddr-audit.sh
# the P3.T12 re-comparison driver: it re-derives the row from the six vendor
# bitstreams the batch already measured, so the summary's claim that no
# further oracle run was spent is checkable.
!oddr-iddr/recompare_rows.py
# the P3.T13/P3.T14 gearbox attribute audit: the driver and its two artefacts.
# It imports P3.T11's decode instrument rather than copying it and spends no
# oracle run, so the OSER/IDES summaries' vendor attribute and fuse tables are
# only auditable with these in the tree. Same named-exception pattern as
# oddr-iddr/audit_oddr_iddr_attrs.py above.
!oser/audit_gearbox_attrs.py
!oser/attr-gap.tsv
!oser/attr-audit.json
